From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:59:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] PROTOTYPE pvr: reuse the SPM scratch buffer for any smaller
 render

Local measurement prototype for amazon-suez, never to be sent. The device
keeps one SPM scratch buffer and reused it only for a render of exactly
the same size, so alternating render sizes created a new one each time:
a kernel buffer of several MB (~9 MB for one full-screen output register
at 1200x1920). Only one partial render runs at a time, so a larger buffer
serves any smaller render.
---
 src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_spm.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_spm.c b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_spm.c
index 9bc8e4d6616..706aa7516b1 100644
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_spm.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_spm.c
@@ -184,7 +184,10 @@ VkResult pvr_spm_scratch_buffer_get_buffer(
     * framebuffers as the scratch buffer is only used during PRs and only one PR
     * can ever be executed at any one time.
     */
-   if (store->head_ref && store->head_ref->size == size) {
+   /* PROTOTYPE: any buffer at least as large will do (one PR at a time, see
+    * above), so renders of different sizes stop reallocating it.
+    */
+   if (store->head_ref && store->head_ref->size >= size) {
       buffer = store->head_ref;
    } else {
       VkResult result;
